# build-kk-integration-cache-cu132.env -- karmic-kraken INTEGRATION (beta
# channel) assembly on the CUDA 13.2 / torch 2.13 aarch64 line, for
# build-spark-cache-cu132.sh. Sibling of build-kk-cache-beta-cu132.env (the
# dev/karmic-kraken + b12x master line); same toolchain except the CuTe DSL.
#
# SOURCE OF THE PIN SET (2026-10-05): the blackwell-llm-docker container
# prerelease karmic-kraken-beta-4102660abd8a98b16e03386a9972a65dbbff805c1527ae7e94ac9c75156445d7
# (image ghcr.io/local-inference-lab/vllm:karmic-kraken-beta-20261005-4102660abd8a98b1,
# digest sha256:fd74019f...; tag commit e881183c, PR #130 glm53-tp4-optimal).
# That image is NGC PyTorch 26.08 / CUDA 13.4.1 / torch 2.14 for linux/amd64
# only and needs an R615 driver for 13.4 features -- not runnable on a Spark
# (aarch64, R580). What it gives us is a QUALIFIED component composition;
# this profile rebuilds those exact component commits on our cu132 line:
#
#   component     release commit   here                  note
#   vllm          f1c2508f         f1c2508f (same)       integration/karmic-kraken-beta
#   b12x          52640cb1         52640cb1 (same)       integration/karmic-kraken-beta
#   lmcache       820af25f         820af25f (same)       = the cache-beta profile
#   instanttensor 95d4729b         95d4729b (same)       = the cache-beta profile
#   flashinfer    LIL dbd6238c     voipmonitor 1ac69427  kept, see toolchain
#   nccl          2.31.2 cu134     2.30.4 cu132          kept (cu132 system-base)
#   torch         2.14 NGC         2.13.0+cu132          kept (cu132 build-base)
#   cutlass-dsl   4.7.1            4.7.1 (was 4.6.2)     REQUIRED by b12x 52640cb1
#
# Release status as published: native GPU and LMCache tests qualified;
# model-serving performance and full GLM cache E2E NOT qualified. Our cu132
# rebuild inherits none of that qualification for torch 2.13 / sm_121.
#
# WHAT THE BETA LINE ADDS over the cache-beta profile (vllm ab86b707 ->
# f1c2508f: +496 commits; b12x ba090286 -> 52640cb1: +248 commits). From the
# .lil/changes fragments, the pair-relevant ones:
#   * Canonical NVFP4-CSF / MXFP4-CSF checkpoints (vllm-956-*, b12x-450): the
#     GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4-MXFP8-CSF-QAD checkpoint loads with --quantization
#     nvfp4_csf --load-format nvfp4_csf; scales stay compressed in VRAM.
#   * W4A16 MoE with NVFP4 prefill activations (vllm-b12x-w4a16-a4-prefill,
#     -a4-prefill-row-type; opt-in via B12X_W4A16_A4_PREFILL_MIN_TOKENS) and
#     CSF scale prefetch (on by default for NVFP4-CSF W4A16).
#   * GLM TP2 memory opt-ins (vllm-898: VLLM_GLM53_EMBED_HOST,
#     VLLM_GLM53_VISION_MXFP8, VLLM_SHARE_PYNCCL_COMMS, ~0.9 GiB/GPU) and
#     weight-load stranding fix with expandable segments (~0.5 GiB/GPU).
#   * External-cache restore admission (vllm-restore-admission; paired with
#     LMCache 820af25f #100-#106): restores wait for capacity instead of
#     recomputing. Fixes for restore/KV-full admission stalls and the TP>=2
#     wait_for_boundary_checkpoint_copies timeout (vllm-950, beta-only bug
#     introduced by vllm-928, fixed in this pin).
#   * Worker failure mid-step exits the server with status 1 (vllm-928): use
#     a container restart policy if you want auto-recovery.
#   * DS4.1 decode drift on SM12x incl. DGX Spark (vllm-943); MiMo-V2.6 DFlash
#     + b12x paged decode; Qwen PLE shared host table (VLLM_PLE_TABLE_MEMORY=
#     shared, b12x-454); Qwen QSA aligned-connector gating (see SparkCache).
#   * CUTLASS DSL 4.7.1 everywhere (vllm-951/-954, b12x 4bacd509+): "The
#     first start after updating compiles B12X kernels again for the new
#     compiler" -- expect a long first boot; the B12X tuning/program cache
#     from the 4.6.2 image does not carry over.
#
# BUILD COST: CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION is an ARG of build-base and base, so this
# profile rebuilds build-base (the 4.6.2 build-base keeps its own tag) and
# every stage after it: FlashInfer AOT, DeepGEMM, b12x, vLLM, final. The
# system-base (CUDA, NCCL 2.30.4) is unchanged and comes from layer cache.
# C++/CUDA objects are mostly ccache hits (the DSL is Python and vLLM's csrc/
# CMake are identical to ab86b707), so this is a re-link, not a cold compile.
#
# PATCH_DEEPGEMM_LIBDW / humming / tokenspeed notes from the cache-beta
# profile apply unchanged (same DeepGEMM ad1f172, same overlay).

IMAGE_REPO=local/vllm
IMAGE_TAG=karmic-kraken-integration-cache-cu132
PROFILE_NAME=kk-integration-cache-cu132

# --- wrapper
LOGGING=1
# PIN_PREFLIGHT=1 also runs the CuTe DSL pre-flight: b12x's exact DSL pin and
# the quack release must agree with CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION before anything builds.
PIN_PREFLIGHT=1
MAX_JOBS=20
VLLM_MAX_JOBS=20
NVCC_THREADS=1
VLLM_NVCC_THREADS=1
PIN_SOURCE_COMMITS=1

# --- serving shape guard (both launchers exist at f1c2508f; only MiMo's
# launcher changed in the delta)
VLLM_REQUIRED_LAUNCHERS=serve-glm53-flash-nvfp4.sh serve-ds4-flash-spark.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sources
# vLLM: integration/karmic-kraken-beta @ f1c2508f (2026-10-05 09:27 +0200,
# merge of PR #982 feat/csf-tp3), the release's vLLM. Descends from
# ab86b707 (merge-base = ab86b707), so everything in the cache-beta profile
# is included. Build-relevant delta: csrc/, cmake/, CMakeLists.txt, setup.py,
# requirements/ are byte-identical to ab86b707; rust/ (tool parsers, built in
# the Rust step) and tools/jovian_wheel_release/ (runtime.lock
# cutlass-dsl.version 4.6.2 -> 4.7.1) changed. FlashInfer module references
# from vllm/ all resolve in the pinned FlashInfer (checked: 67 import sites).
# The branch tip is already past this (41aa7cea on 2026-10-06); stay on the
# release commit -- it is the composition the release qualified.
VLLM_REPO=https://github.com/local-inference-lab/vllm.git
VLLM_PIN=f1c2508f1018f47ee8a78478a819d202f359887b

# B12X: integration/karmic-kraken-beta @ 52640cb1 (2026-10-04 21:41 +0200,
# PR #479 perf/w4a8-mxfp4-csf-inline), the release's b12x. = master a321f9a6
# + the beta composition (CSF: Nvfp4CsfWeights / CsfScalePlanes /
# Mxfp4CsfWeights, W4A16 A4 prefill, MXFP8 W8A8 MoE, PLE caller-provided
# host tables, collective barrier fixes). Contains ba090286, so the winner-
# artifact exchange vLLM needs is present. pyproject pins
# nvidia-cutlass-dsl{,-libs-base,-libs-core,-libs-cu12,-libs-cu13}==4.7.1
# EXACTLY -- the reason CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION moves below.
B12X_REPO=https://github.com/local-inference-lab/b12x.git
B12X_PIN=52640cb15d4ad1c7230f747e72c45d45dc2da681

# DeepGEMM: KK's vendored pin is still ad1f172 at f1c2508f
# (cmake/external_projects/deepgemm.cmake).
DEEPGEMM_REPO=https://github.com/vllm-project/DeepGEMM.git
DEEPGEMM_REF=ad1f1726aa540a76c1d26d6a120effb8de21eaa4
DEEPGEMM_COMMIT=ad1f1726aa540a76c1d26d6a120effb8de21eaa4

# InstantTensor: the release's pin (instanttensor-cu134-beta-95d4729b...).
INSTANTTENSOR_REPO=https://github.com/local-inference-lab/InstantTensor.git
INSTANTTENSOR_REF=95d4729b6d6a991bb8de61877147a9d9d9100b23
INSTANTTENSOR_COMMIT=95d4729b6d6a991bb8de61877147a9d9d9100b23

# LMCache: the release's pin, identical to the cache-beta profile
# (integration/local-inference-lab @ 820af25f; 430 passed / 19 skipped on the
# CPU suite, 2026-10-03). It carries the restore-admission half that this
# vLLM's vllm-restore-admission pairs with (ef929e16 gates it on the vLLM API,
# so on ab86b707 it fell back; here it engages). PATCH_LMCACHE_INTEGRATION's
# 26-file test list is unchanged.
LMCACHE_REPO=https://github.com/local-inference-lab/LMCache.git
LMCACHE_REF=820af25ff630f4c00f7faefbcc31bc5ccd7bab71
LMCACHE_COMMIT=820af25ff630f4c00f7faefbcc31bc5ccd7bab71
LMCACHE_BUILD_VERSION=0.5.3.dev425+lil.820af25f
PATCH_LMCACHE_INTEGRATION=on

# SparkCache: same package pin as cache-beta (801f7f9a, still main HEAD).
# The vLLM patches are REBASED for f1c2508f -- separate files, because the
# wrapper requires each file's SparkCache-vLLM-Pin header to equal VLLM_PIN
# (the e77be225 files stay for the cache-beta profile):
#   01-vmm-exemption       REQUIRED. Same hunk; applies at +43 lines. This
#                          vLLM adds SupportsVmmSafeTransfers, the proper
#                          mechanism -- the patch can go once SparkCache's
#                          connector declares it.
#   02-shared-prefix-lease optional. scheduler.py and kv_cache_manager.py
#                          gained restore admission (+292/+414 lines). Two
#                          hand fixes on top of the 3-way merge: lease eviction
#                          and the free-block checks include import_reserve,
#                          and the lease attach runs after the external-
#                          boundary admission gate. Applies with zero fuzz;
#                          every manager/coordinator API it calls is unchanged.
#                          Still NOT runtime-tested, as before.
# Model constraints at this vLLM (enforced at engine start, not by the image):
#   GLM: unchanged -- SparkCache (aligned) needs REPLAYSSM=0, because KDA
#        recovery requires an atomic request-boundary connector.
#   Qwen3.8 (QSA): NEW -- any KV connector must be request-boundary, or
#        --recurrent-checkpoint-policy aligned + DCP1 + a connector that
#        declares supports_aligned_hybrid_transfer (only SimpleCPUOffload /
#        Offloading do). SparkCache does not, so Qwen + SparkCache is refused.
SPARKCACHE_REPO=https://github.com/FujitsuPolycom/sparkcache
SPARKCACHE_COMMIT=801f7f9a4bd83de8fddc35bda721089acf16584a
SPARKCACHE_VLLM_PATCHES=sparkcache-vllm-f1c2508f-01-vmm-exemption.patch,sparkcache-vllm-f1c2508f-02-shared-prefix-lease.patch
PATCH_SPARKCACHE=on

# fastokens: unchanged (0.3.2). f1c2508f keeps VLLM_USE_FASTOKENS and
# _MIN_FASTOKENS_VERSION=0.2.0.
FASTOKENS_VERSION=0.3.2
FASTOKENS_SHA256=cbb29fae028d39a2020d01dfe587e1774a516b6d28641b70e83a285d460bdfb8
PATCH_FASTOKENS=on

# exllamav3: unchanged (EXL3 path, unrelated to GLM/KK).
EXLLAMAV3_COMMIT=704aefd743b390af4bd0fb429d1906f9b964c7d8

# ------------------------------------------------------------- toolchain
# Identical to build-kk-cache-beta-cu132.env EXCEPT the CuTe DSL pair
# (CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION, QUACK_KERNELS_SPEC). torch, NCCL and the cu132
# system-base are the driver-proven line and stay.
TORCH_VERSION=2.13.0+cu132
TORCHVISION_VERSION=0.28.0+cu132
TORCH_BUNDLED_NCCL_VERSION=2.29.7
NCCL_REPO=https://github.com/local-inference-lab/nccl-canonical.git
NCCL_REF=canonical/cu132-nccl2304-amd-noxml
NCCL_COMMIT=dfab7c1ace32da250ba97757879429c341b7bcf9
# FlashInfer: KEPT at voipmonitor 1ac69427 (0.6.18), not the release's LIL
# dbd6238c. Reasons: (1) dbd6238c ships a 414-file flashinfer/b12x migration
# snapshot + b12x entry points that the release assembler strips and our
# Dockerfile does not -- it would compete with the real b12x package;
# (2) it is the cu134-sm120 line (283 commits ahead), unbuilt on cu132/sm_121;
# (3) 1ac69427 declares nvidia-cutlass-dsl>=4.5.0, so 4.7.1 installs cleanly,
# and LIL's own 4.7.1 move (efd67581) was a pin-only change with no code
# edits. Risk that remains: FlashInfer's CuTe-DSL kernels run under 4.7.1
# untested on this commit. GLM/Qwen serve attention/MoE/linear on b12x, so
# FlashInfer is on the sampler / DFlash-drafter / DS4 paths only.
FLASHINFER_REPO=https://github.com/voipmonitor/flashinfer.git
FLASHINFER_REF=integration/main-pr4393-pcie-ipc-qualified-20260807
FLASHINFER_COMMIT=1ac6942776b383c6b03c7a5805a22e72a3e3349f
FLASHINFER_BUILD_CUBIN=0
# CUTLASS (C++ source for FlashInfer's stage): unchanged. Its
# blockscaled_layout.py override is byte-identical to the one inside DSL
# 4.6.2 AND 4.7.1 (sha256 e9627e0d..., sm120_make_smem_layout_sfa present in
# both), so the FlashInfer stage's copy stays a no-op on 4.7.1.
CUTLASS_REF=e6233cbac5d7c7a865c19c91cd684ceece19513c
CUTLASS_COMMIT=e6233cbac5d7c7a865c19c91cd684ceece19513c
# CHANGED: 4.6.2 -> 4.7.1. b12x 52640cb1 pins ==4.7.1 (base, libs-base,
# libs-core, libs-cu12, libs-cu13); vLLM f1c2508f's runtime.lock says 4.7.1;
# requirements/cuda.txt already said 4.7.1. PyPI has cp312
# manylinux_2_28_aarch64 wheels for libs-base, libs-cu12 and libs-cu13;
# nvidia-cutlass-dsl and libs-core are pure Python (checked 2026-10-06).
CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.7.1
TILELANG_VERSION=0.1.12
TOKENSPEED_MLA_VERSION=0.1.8
TVM_FFI_VERSION=0.1.11
# CHANGED: 0.6.4 -> 0.6.5. quack 0.6.4 requires nvidia-cutlass-dsl==4.6.2;
# 0.6.5 requires >=4.7 and is what vLLM's cuda.txt names (FIX_FULL's quack
# re-pin becomes a no-op). Other deps identical (torch, apache-tvm-ffi<0.2,
# torch-c-dlpack-ext, einops). tilelang 0.1.12 / tokenspeed-mla 0.1.8 /
# humming 0.1.12 / apache-tvm-ffi 0.1.11 place no conflicting DSL pin.
QUACK_KERNELS_SPEC=quack-kernels==0.6.5
FASTSAFETENSORS_SPEC=fastsafetensors>=0.3.3
HUMMING_KERNELS_SPEC=humming-kernels[cu13]==0.1.12
XGRAMMAR_REF=v0.2.5
XGRAMMAR_COMMIT=2ea71da4ccb997a06928c9fb69b99f330da56697
XGRAMMAR_VERSION=0.2.5
XGRAMMAR_TRANSFORMERS5_COMPAT=1
VLLM_RUNTIME_EXTRA_PACKAGES=nvtx==0.2.15 nccl4py==0.3.1

# ------------------------------------------------------------ patch toggles
# Same as build-kk-cache-beta-cu132.env (see its comments). The io_uring
# seccomp profile at f1c2508f is byte-identical to ab86b707 (sha256
# 823b66051a52...), so a node already configured for the cache-beta image
# needs no daemon change.
PATCH_GPU_ARCH=auto
PATCH_HOST_ARCH=auto
PATCH_PCIE_ENV=auto
PATCH_PIPCHECK_WHEELTAG=auto
PATCH_VLLM_REQ_MARKERS=auto
PATCH_VLLM_WHEEL_TAGS=auto
PATCH_EXLLAMAV3_AVX=auto
PATCH_DEEPGEMM_LIBDW=on
PATCH_IO_URING=on
